# Copy to .env, then uncomment and edit the lines you want. The Makefile loads
# this file into the environment for make run and friends; the binary itself
# never reads it (containers pass -e or --env-file instead).
#
# Rules: one bare KEY=value per line; no quotes, no trailing comments (they
# leave trailing spaces in the value); write $$ for a literal $. A value set
# here beats the same variable in your shell for make targets; for a one-off
# override use a make variable instead: make run TODO_ADDR=127.0.0.1:9090
#
# Every line below is commented out, so a fresh copy changes nothing: an unset
# or empty variable keeps its default, which is the value shown.
#TODO_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080
#TODO_LOG_LEVEL=info
#TODO_LOG_FORMAT=text
#TODO_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT=10s
